WEBVTT

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.309
A dream...

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.429
Been a while since I last had that one.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.439
Master Hiraku!

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:45.229
Pardon me, I still haven't
prepared anything for breakfast...

00:00:45.789 --> 00:00:46.979
No, it's okay.

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:48.950
I just happened to get up early today.

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:51.450
Also,

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:54.200
I'd rather you stop calling me Master.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:56.310
I see.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:57.829
Village Chief.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.670
Good morning!

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.329
Morning.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.620
I let my guard down...

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.219
You've finally touched the kitchen...

00:01:12.329 --> 00:01:13.829
I'll just burn the thing wholesale.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.629
No, just spare the thing.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.170
Oh?

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.739
You're up pretty early today, aren't you?

00:01:28.739 --> 00:01:31.420
Somehow I just woke up.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.819
Good morning!

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.239
What's up?

00:01:37.239 --> 00:01:40.500
I had a bit of business
with Gran Maria on my rounds.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.980
A trouble?

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.819
Not at all, but we've been
receiving reports about this...

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.260
Can I help you?

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.010
Well... You see...

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.370
I had this dream again
last night after a while.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.010
Dream?

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.810
Or maybe...

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:00.299
A memory from my past, I think.

00:02:01.519 --> 00:02:04.019
Hey, wait up!

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.319
Really...

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.000
The me back then wouldn't
have been able to imagine this.

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:44.150
For me to live a dreamlike,
cozy life like this.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.819
FARMING LIFE IN ANOTHER WORLD

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.569
Hiraku Machio...

00:04:19.569 --> 00:04:21.360
I assume it's your name?

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:22.579
Yes.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.629
Um, who are you?

00:04:24.629 --> 00:04:27.079
I am the god who governs the world.

00:04:27.389 --> 00:04:28.500
God?

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:31.519
So I finally died, huh.

00:04:31.519 --> 00:04:32.339
Indeed you did.

00:04:32.339 --> 00:04:35.439
According to this world's calendar,
you've lived for 39 years.

00:04:35.439 --> 00:04:37.589
Your life was nothing
but too great hardships.

00:04:37.959 --> 00:04:41.589
Betrayed by others,
and collapsing from a terminal illness.

00:04:41.589 --> 00:04:46.019
Hence, I mean to give you
another chance for life.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.259
You can do that?

00:04:48.259 --> 00:04:53.360
But of course. I shall provide you
with a healthy body free of any illnesses.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:58.329
Truth be told, the reason you
had to live such a cruel life...

00:04:58.329 --> 00:05:00.439
...was partly a mistake of mine too.

00:05:00.439 --> 00:05:01.110
Mistake?

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:04.529
Would you consider this
an atonement for that?

00:05:05.839 --> 00:05:08.730
I don't really get it,
but sure.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.370
While we're at it,
do you have any request?

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.949
I shall have you live your new life
the way you see fit.

00:05:14.949 --> 00:05:16.319
The way I see fit...

00:05:16.319 --> 00:05:18.920
I can fulfill most requests.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:21.490
In that case...
All right.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.889
I want to try farming, Sir!

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.509
Farming?

00:05:24.509 --> 00:05:29.000
When I was trapped in my bed in the hospital,
I used to love watching this show on TV.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.139
It was about an idol's farming experience!

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:35.069
I couldn't be so sociable in my previous life,

00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:37.680
so I'd love to do some farming...

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.829
...in a place far from civilisation, peacefully...

00:05:41.439 --> 00:05:42.720
Can't I?

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.910
Well, agriculture has a different jurisdiction...

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:45.910
Jurisdiction?

00:05:46.519 --> 00:05:48.410
But I'll have a word with him.

00:05:48.829 --> 00:05:50.860
Ah, hm, okay.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.920
All right.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:57.459
I shall bestow you with a new life
and a healthy body.

00:05:57.459 --> 00:06:00.600
And I have acquired the permission
from the God of Farming,

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.430
so I shall bestow you with
the "Omnipotent Farming Tool" power.

00:06:04.019 --> 00:06:05.610
Omnipotent Farming Tool?

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:06.300
Well, then.

00:06:07.569 --> 00:06:10.519
Enjoy your second life
to the fullest now.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:30.240
I can move my body...

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:35.149
Been a while since I moved my body.

00:06:35.149 --> 00:06:37.079
Who knows how long I missed standing.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:42.339
A healthy body really rocks!

00:06:44.589 --> 00:06:47.470
All right, now that I'm back alive,

00:06:48.529 --> 00:06:50.589
I'll live my second life here...

00:06:50.589 --> 00:06:53.540
...doing what I longed for long, farming!

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:02.860
So this is the starting point?

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.860
GRASP THE CURRENT REALITY

00:07:06.709 --> 00:07:10.370
A forest... As far as I can see,
I'm surrounded with trees.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:14.230
Sure, I did ask for a place away
from civilisation,

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:17.699
but isn't this too far from it
that people won't actually come here?

00:07:17.699 --> 00:07:20.189
There's no point in lamenting it.

00:07:20.189 --> 00:07:22.379
Let's think of what I can do for now.

00:07:23.279 --> 00:07:25.879
My getup is just like one
of those villagers in a game.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.680
I think I somehow became young again too.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.060
Is there anything I can use?

00:07:31.779 --> 00:07:34.139
Oh, right!
The Omnipotent Farming Tool...

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.019
This is it?

00:07:42.839 --> 00:07:44.300
One, two!

00:07:46.319 --> 00:07:48.529
Is this some kind of magical force?

00:07:48.529 --> 00:07:50.600
I keep swinging,
but I never get tired,

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:54.040
and it can plough through hard ground
and tree roots without a care in the world.

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.040
The soil is so fluffy.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:01.259
I could grow good
vegetables if I planted a field with it.

00:08:01.259 --> 00:08:04.800
Wait, I need to secure water
and food first before that.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:07.800
EXPLORE THE SURROUNDING AREA

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:10.819
Exploring the forest again.

00:08:10.819 --> 00:08:13.180
I've been listening around for a river,

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:16.310
but all I can hear is the sound of leaves.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.959
Let alone edible plants,

00:08:19.959 --> 00:08:21.810
I can't even find a single grass.

00:08:22.139 --> 00:08:23.389
Am I on the right difficulty?

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.129
Now that I think of it,

00:08:29.129 --> 00:08:32.100
it's no surprise if I encounter
a dangerous monster here.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.200
I need to find a place
where I can settle down, quick.

00:08:43.519 --> 00:08:45.460
What a big tree...

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:50.470
It'll make for a good landmark,
so I'll just set up a base here for now.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:53.470
SECURE SOME MATERIALS

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:55.659
I wandered around a fair bit,

00:08:55.659 --> 00:08:58.429
but looks like I couldn't
find any river or pond nearby.

00:08:58.899 --> 00:08:59.730
Then...

00:09:00.519 --> 00:09:01.480
I'll just dig a well!

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:02.730
DOWSING - A METHOD OF FINDING HIDDEN UNDERGROUND
OBJECTS BY THE MOVEMENT OF A STICK OR PENDULUM

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:06.539
It would seem reckless to search
for water veins with these, I bet.

00:09:06.909 --> 00:09:12.100
But this method has been used to
find water pipes... or not.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.240
I don't really get it.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:15.370
Shovel!

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.139
This "Omnipotent Farming Tool" skill...

00:09:19.139 --> 00:09:21.250
...really does take shape
into all kinds of tools.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:22.500
- By the way, I can't create complicated machines.
- Excavator!

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.000
- By the way, I can't create complicated machines.
- The big stuff!

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:29.879
As expected, I don't feel tired
at all just like with the hoe!

00:09:30.789 --> 00:09:33.480
I can dig forever
until I find water like this!

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:37.139
I can't get out...

00:09:37.139 --> 00:09:38.570
Fine, then!

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.059
I'll just dig in diagonally!

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:50.149
I dug a water source first try!
What luck!

00:09:50.919 --> 00:09:54.409
This may be thanks to the God.

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.909
Water secured, moving on to food now.
However...

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.710
Surprisingly, I don't feel hungry at all.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.399
Is this also the power
of the Omnipotent Farming Tool?

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:09.919
It'll be dangerous to wander
around the forest again too.

00:10:09.919 --> 00:10:11.009
Scythe!

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:16.730
I should keep using my Omnipotent Farming
Tool here while building a proper base.

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:19.929
I hope I can find something edible
along the way too...

00:10:20.889 --> 00:10:23.379
Well, couldn't find anything.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.570
I'll be cultivating a field here soon,

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:31.440
and this tree will get in the way, I guess.

00:10:32.649 --> 00:10:34.830
It looks so sturdy,

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:37.450
but I guess my axe can chop it down.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:40.610
I think I should make a cut to one side,

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:43.669
and then another on the other side, huh?

00:10:43.669 --> 00:10:44.460
Sweet!

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.330
All right, let's start from this side first.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:54.970
Huh?

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:09.720
In a single slash, huh?
This skill does live up to its name.

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:11.500
Hatchet!

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.879
Now that I've chopped it down,
let's try processing it.

00:11:14.879 --> 00:11:18.120
Strip off the branches, cut the trees into logs,
and peel the bark off.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.720
The hard wood cuts through
like cheese with this.

00:11:22.429 --> 00:11:26.370
By the way, about this hook thing
that I'm using to drag the log.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.090
I don't know the name,

00:11:28.090 --> 00:11:31.870
but as long as I can picture it,
the Omnipotent Farming Tool can transform into it.

00:11:32.679 --> 00:11:34.879
I could make some timber
to some extent.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:39.889
In the sandbox game I used to play,
now should be the time to build a hut,

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:43.990
but I couldn't just make the parts
for the walls and roof with a snap.

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.409
I don't even have any nails nor adhesives.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.899
Is it actually that hard
to build a hut from scratch?

00:11:50.409 --> 00:11:53.320
Ah... The shadow coming
from the pillar I built...

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.720
It's just like a clock.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:00.240
Oh, shoot! I was too absorbed in this,
I lost track of time!

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.100
At this rate, the sun will set!
And then what happens?!

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:05.519
It'll get dark!
I need to find a source of light!

00:12:05.519 --> 00:12:07.159
Flashlight! Lamp!

00:12:07.159 --> 00:12:09.169
No dice, huh?
I'll just start a fire, then!

00:12:09.169 --> 00:12:10.669
Lighter! Match!

00:12:10.669 --> 00:12:14.419
Oh, shoot! Is this because of the jurisdiction
thing the God mentioned earlier?

00:12:14.419 --> 00:12:18.519
Besides, if I turn this Omnipotent Farming Tool
into a match, I could actually lose it!

00:12:18.519 --> 00:12:21.629
Something that generates
heat without depleting it...

00:12:21.629 --> 00:12:22.429
That's right!

00:12:22.429 --> 00:12:23.759
Magnifying glass!

00:12:24.679 --> 00:12:27.179
Success! Now I can start a fire!

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.820
If only it weren't sunset already...

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:39.450
I hastily dug a hole in the trunk
as a temporary shelter.

00:12:40.149 --> 00:12:44.700
I also thought of digging in the ground,
but I could be buried alive, so I decided not to.

00:12:45.059 --> 00:12:48.539
This chisel is also shaped
from the Omnipotent Farming Tool,

00:12:49.519 --> 00:12:51.820
but I guess in order to build
a hut and its furniture,

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:54.210
trial and error is needed.

00:12:55.879 --> 00:12:57.980
I thought I'd be doomed
when it got dark,

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.360
but I still surprisingly
could see well at night.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:04.389
Must be because the God gave me a healthy body,
so I got great eyesight.

00:13:04.389 --> 00:13:05.470
Or...

00:13:06.139 --> 00:13:09.730
Maybe it's because of the two moons above.

00:13:11.529 --> 00:13:12.480
I really...

00:13:13.629 --> 00:13:15.460
...did come to another world, huh.

00:13:17.529 --> 00:13:19.990
WELL - PILLAR - TRUNK CAVE

00:13:24.129 --> 00:13:28.539
While I was processing the timber
through trial and error, the sun came.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:40.110
Well, the water's good enough for now.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.759
Oh, right!
Before I forget!

00:13:48.159 --> 00:13:50.269
Fire secured as well.

00:13:50.269 --> 00:13:51.169
Whoop, whoop!

00:13:51.169 --> 00:13:55.019
I continued clearing the area for the field.

00:13:55.019 --> 00:13:59.389
While I don't feel tired or hungry
when chopping down a lot of trees with this tool,

00:13:59.389 --> 00:14:03.289
I still use my energy between each work.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.029
Many a little makes a mickle.

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:09.769
In other words,
I'm getting hungry now.

00:14:09.769 --> 00:14:13.789
Maybe I'll change my policy and go looking
for food, even if I have to travel a long way.

00:14:19.049 --> 00:14:20.549
Wh-What is that thing?!

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.179
What an unfortunate accident...

00:14:30.919 --> 00:14:32.590
Well, it is what it is.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:34.919
It looked so scary with those fangs...

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:38.690
And I hit the thing with the scythe
from the tool to the neck.

00:14:39.149 --> 00:14:42.950
I ploughed the giant rabbit's head,
and it became one with the fluffy soil.

00:14:43.559 --> 00:14:47.200
I dissected the remaining body
with the knife shaped by the tool.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:50.720
I'll just accept this meat
as my food gratefully.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.200
Grilled rabbit...

00:14:53.879 --> 00:14:55.960
It tastes like Mother Nature.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.019
It also reeks blood.

00:14:58.019 --> 00:15:00.710
But I should be grateful
that this is at least edible.

00:15:02.169 --> 00:15:05.200
Whatever comes in will come out later.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.970
I made a toilet next for that purpose.

00:15:07.929 --> 00:15:09.470
The seat is made from a round log,

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:10.259
TOILET SEAT - TANK - GAS DRAINAGE - PUMPING HOLE

00:15:10.259 --> 00:15:12.720
TOILET SEAT - TANK - GAS DRAINAGE - PUMPING HOLE
and there's a hole in it.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.480
I can do my business in peace now.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:25.779
Or not.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.529
I tried to use the building techniques
I thought about without sleeping.

00:15:30.039 --> 00:15:32.289
It looks grander than my sleeping block,

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:36.789
but in a civilised lifestyle,
a pleasant toilet is irreplaceable!

00:15:41.879 --> 00:15:45.809
I made a lot of detours,
but I'm finally ploughing me a field.

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:49.940
What should I grow here to make a living?

00:15:50.450 --> 00:15:54.450
Something that can be well-preserved...
Potatoes? Onions?

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:57.940
Tomato and cucumbers sound nice too.
I can eat them raw.

00:15:58.309 --> 00:16:02.409
Cabbages, spinach, radish, bok choy, carrots.

00:16:02.409 --> 00:16:05.320
Oh, I want to boil some corn and eat it!

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:09.200
I knew it deep down.

00:16:10.159 --> 00:16:13.950
Even with all these fields, I don't have
the seeds to fill them, nor the seedlings.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:18.210
I guess I'll just have to find
something in the forest after all.

00:16:19.029 --> 00:16:22.210
After eating a rabbit and taking a rest,

00:16:23.409 --> 00:16:25.710
I was left awestruck
with amazement the next morning.

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.220
Wha...

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:31.059
Do plants in this world grow without seeds?

00:16:31.059 --> 00:16:33.470
Or is it thanks to
the Omnipotent Farming Tool?

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:36.980
There are sprouts in every row!

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:40.600
But they are in different
states of development.

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:43.480
That looks like... green onion?
Kind of bent, though.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.940
Well, I don't know what's what,

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.490
but I know what to do now!

00:16:48.929 --> 00:16:52.990
I'll protect these fields from the giant rabbits
and other monsters I haven't encountered yet!

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:57.250
I'll first build a fence around the area.

00:16:57.929 --> 00:17:00.490
Next, I'll dig a trench outside the fence.

00:17:01.409 --> 00:17:04.500
I still have my worries,
but it's better than nothing.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:09.009
In a few days, both the fence
and the trench are complete.

00:17:09.009 --> 00:17:13.509
In the meantime, I made do with food by taking down
the rabbits that tried to attack me again.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:16.349
Why do they go straight to me?

00:17:16.349 --> 00:17:18.269
I guess they want to eat me?

00:17:21.329 --> 00:17:22.519
Mother Nature...

00:17:23.859 --> 00:17:26.509
The sprouts are growing bigger
each day with the water....

00:17:26.509 --> 00:17:28.480
...from the watering pot shaped by the tool.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.859
It seems to hasten their growth
than just simply planting them.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:37.359
I still don't know what they are,
but I hope they're something edible.

00:17:37.359 --> 00:17:39.660
If all of them turn out
to be decorative plants...

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:45.670
I'm confident I'll collapse to my knees.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.670
And another few days later.

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:51.430
After much struggle,
I finally managed to build a hut.

00:17:52.259 --> 00:17:55.430
A so-called log cabin,
dug and stacked in a wooden trench.

00:17:56.859 --> 00:17:59.180
I couldn't bring the timber higher halfway,

00:18:00.049 --> 00:18:03.190
so I dug the ground inside
down to gain height.

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:07.980
The roof is made of tree bark and held in place
with nails made from shavings of wood.

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:13.450
In fairytales, this would've been
easily blown away by the wolf,

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:16.200
but it's far more civilised
than living in a trunk.

00:18:17.529 --> 00:18:20.470
It's also fun to see the crops growing.

00:18:21.279 --> 00:18:24.539
I'm suddenly motivated
and enjoy every day.

00:18:25.579 --> 00:18:29.410
And just when my life here
started to take off...

00:18:32.869 --> 00:18:33.839
Dogs?

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:35.839
They're really big.

00:18:36.789 --> 00:18:39.059
They don't seem to want to attack me.

00:18:39.059 --> 00:18:41.720
Also, they're wounded here and there.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.109
Come here.

00:18:51.519 --> 00:18:55.109
I just happened to take down a boar
and didn't know what to do with the meat.

00:18:55.849 --> 00:18:59.119
It was trying to climb over the fence,
so I had to take it down.

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:02.410
The other dog has a bulging stomach.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:07.130
I guess the male dog was taking her with him,
and they got attacked by a monster.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:12.200
I remember wanting to have
a dog when I was a kid.

00:19:12.839 --> 00:19:17.529
They say dogs are the allies of farmers,
so I'll be happy if they stick with me.

00:19:19.509 --> 00:19:21.339
Huh? What's up?

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:24.019
Wait a second!

00:19:24.019 --> 00:19:25.519
She's going to give birth?!

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:27.299
Right here?!

00:19:27.799 --> 00:19:28.720
What do I do?

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:30.519
What should I do?!

00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:32.529
For now,

00:19:32.529 --> 00:19:35.529
I took them to the log cabin
since it'll be safer.

00:19:36.589 --> 00:19:38.990
How long does it take for a delivery?

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.890
Does she need water?

00:19:41.799 --> 00:19:44.500
It's cold after sunset,
so I should light a bonfire.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:45.990
But then it'll smoke...

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.539
I'll just place it by the entrance...

00:19:53.609 --> 00:19:54.839
Anyway,

00:19:54.839 --> 00:19:57.049
I did what I could.

00:19:57.049 --> 00:20:00.950
I thought it'd be bad for a human
to stay nearby, so I retreated here.

00:20:03.029 --> 00:20:05.210
Did I get in their way...

00:20:05.210 --> 00:20:07.319
...by doing something I shouldn't?

00:20:07.869 --> 00:20:12.069
What if that big boar attacked again
while they couldn't move?

00:20:15.819 --> 00:20:18.250
I don't know if it's because of the bonfire,

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:20.480
but the sky is looking darker now.

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.329
Shoot! I fell asleep!

00:20:37.549 --> 00:20:39.670
I'm coming in.

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:48.559
It sure looks relieving when it's over,

00:20:48.559 --> 00:20:51.079
but the mother must've had it rough.

00:20:51.079 --> 00:20:51.859
Right.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:57.859
I cut the best part of the boar
to celebrate her delivery.

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:03.869
I thought they'd be going somewhere
after they were done,

00:21:04.259 --> 00:21:06.369
but looks like they're enjoying it here.

00:21:07.319 --> 00:21:11.630
I feel bad if I have to kick them out of that hut
when they've already settled in,

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.390
so I built another.

00:21:15.039 --> 00:21:17.880
I'd like to think that this is
an improvement compared to my last.

00:21:18.569 --> 00:21:20.880
When the pups start running around,

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.890
the crops are properly ready to harvest now.

00:21:24.559 --> 00:21:26.119
Tomatoes.

00:21:26.119 --> 00:21:28.640
If left alone,
they would have become bushes.

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:32.750
It's hard to harvest it,
and the fruit is small too.

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:36.650
But it's a proper tomato.

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:39.400
The dogs hunt for game,

00:21:39.849 --> 00:21:42.160
and patrol the surroundings.

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:43.160
Calling them "dogs" would be hard,

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:45.319
KURO - YUKI
Calling them "dogs" would be hard,

00:21:45.319 --> 00:21:47.150
KURO - YUKI
so I decided to name them.

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:49.420
KUROICHI - KURONI - KUROSAN - KUROYON
The male one's Kuro, the female Yuki.

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:50.660
They're all black, though.

00:21:51.049 --> 00:21:52.450
Kuro, Yuki.

00:21:54.509 --> 00:21:56.920
I didn't think they'd eat vegetables,

00:21:57.440 --> 00:21:59.670
but when I see them eating
the tomatoes so happily,

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:03.430
it makes me want to feed
them more delicious vegetables.

00:22:04.549 --> 00:22:08.410
I'm getting busy with the harvest,
and scream happily.

00:22:08.869 --> 00:22:11.180
I need to make a storage hut for these.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:13.299
And also furniture and tools.

00:22:14.170 --> 00:22:16.220
I still got a lot of things to do, but...

00:22:18.470 --> 00:22:20.869
Well, I'll just do my best...

00:22:21.839 --> 00:22:23.680
...slowly, and peacefully.

00:22:25.529 --> 00:22:28.910
FENCE AND TRENCH - WELL
- HUT 1 - HUT 2 - TOILET - FIELD

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:22.710
Going through the mountains?

00:23:23.059 --> 00:23:27.220
You don't want to say that
unless you're drunk, Miss.

00:23:27.579 --> 00:23:30.009
Have you ever heard
of the "Forest of Death"?

00:23:30.009 --> 00:23:32.470
Beyond the mountains is
that very infamous forest.

00:23:33.079 --> 00:23:34.960
It's full of dangerous monsters.

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:38.329
If those monsters attack,
their numbers will be too large,

00:23:38.329 --> 00:23:40.930
we must stand guard
at all hours of the day in the village.

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:44.940
All the more reason, then.

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:50.950
EPISODE 2: THE FIRST VILLAGER
